## Findings
- **Login & Roles**: Successful login for `instructor@example.com`. However, the UI displays "STUDENT" role in the top right, while still providing instructor links in the sidebar. Newly registered accounts default to "STUDENT" and lack instructor links entirely.
- **Course Management**: Instructor can successfully view, create (`New Test Course`), and edit basic information (Title, Description, Level, Price).
- **Curriculum Functionality**: The "Add Section" button in the Course Curriculum section is visible (with index 34 in DOM and clearly shown in screenshots) but completely unresponsive across multiple courses and account attempts.
- **API/Permissions**: Observed multiple 403 Forbidden errors in the browser console for `GET /api/courses` and `GET /api/courses/[id]`, indicating possible RBAC or tenant isolation issues that may be affecting curriculum sub-resources.
- **UI Consistency**: The "Course Curriculum" section is only displayed when editing an existing course, not during the initial course creation flow.
